{
 "_doc": "Battle HUD per era (docs/ERA_FEEL_HUD.md), read by scripts/battle/presenter/EraBattleHud.gd. One entry per era I-V; every era sets every key in EraBattleHud.KEYS. The HUD follows the jump in handheld technology: Era I plain ink boxes and a text menu, Era II limited colour and marks, Era III styled slanted plates and element-coloured art buttons, Era IV large touch buttons with details, Era V moving plates and rolling numbers. Paper and ink always come from UITheme (high contrast and the era skin of data/era_feel.json win); accent, light and shade are this era's HUD colours. font: pixel or large. frame: frame kind of the battle text box and the command panel. plate_*: name plate shape. bar_h: Vigor bar height. pip: Energy pip size. marks: bonded-before mark and Gleam/Prism mark on the plate. hp_numbers: plain or roll. xp: static (jumps) or fill (animated). menu: text (cursor list), buttons, typed (element-coloured) or touch (large, two lines). commands: grid (2 by 2 words) or row. art_h, command_h: row heights. art_detail: element name and matchup word on the art button. item_shortcut: a button that uses the last item again. info_card: plain or rich long-press card. team_*: the team row (one mark per team member, never a round shape). level_panel: list, delta (gain in colour) or bars. level_count: numbers count up. bond: look of the Echo call screen. bond_mark: mark size there. mini: look of the small tags in formation battles (fit = as wide as the sprite). camera_follow: share of the battle camera's move the plates follow.",
